Algorithm / Procedure
A. Straight-through Cable
1. Cut the UTP cable to the required length using a cable cutter.
2. Remove approximately 2–3 cm of the outer insulation.
3. Arrange the eight wires in the T568B color sequence.
4. Straighten the wires and trim them evenly.
5. Insert the wires into the RJ-45 connector, ensuring each wire reaches its correct pin.
6. Use the crimping tool to fix the connector firmly.
7. Repeat the same T568B wiring sequence at the other end.
8. Test the cable using a LAN cable tester.
B. Crossover Cable
1. Cut the UTP cable to the required length.
2. Strip the outer insulation at both ends.
3. Arrange the wires at the first end according to T568A.
4. Insert the wires into an RJ-45 connector and crimp it.
5. Arrange the wires at the second end according to T568B.
6. Insert the wires into the second RJ-45 connector and crimp it.
7. Test the cable using a LAN cable tester.
8. Verify that the cable follows the crossover wiring arrangement.
